  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The first term of an arithmetic series is ${a}_{1}=5,$ the common difference is $d=-2.5,$ and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=-105.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the number of terms, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d).\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${a}_{1}=5$, $d=-2.5$ and ${S}_{N}=-105$ into the above and solve for $N$, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -105 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 5+(N-1)\\cdot (-2.5)) \\\\ -210 & =N(10-2.5N+2.5) \\\\ -210 & =12.5N-2.5{N}^{2} \\\\ 2.5{N}^{2}-12.5N-210 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-(-12.5)\\pm \\sqrt{(-12.5)^{2}-4\\cdot 2.5\\cdot (-210)}}{2\\cdot 2.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12.5\\pm 47.5}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $N=12$ or $N=-7.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=12$ terms.",
